// Title: Sysprep on AppData Folder
// Sigma ID: d5b9ae7a-e6fc-405e-80ff-2ff9dcc64e7e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2018-06-22 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects suspicious sysprep process start with AppData folder as target (as used by Trojan
//   Syndicasec in Thrip report by Symantec)
// False positives:
//   - False positives depend on scripts and administrative tools used in the monitored environment
// References:
//   - https://www.symantec.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/thrip-hits-satellite-telecoms-defense-targets
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/61a296bb-81ad-4fee-955f-3b399f4aaf4b
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysprep_appdata.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\sysprep.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\"
